### name: review.order.sort-over-a-projection-of-sorted-rows-is-refused
--- note
JS-C59 family (orderDropped): a derived table with no LIMIT beside its ORDER BY does not keep
the order, and the earlier sort is the later one's tie-break. Refused at the second sort;
Emitting `SELECT _sub1.* FROM (... ORDER BY amount) _sub1 ORDER BY name` would lose the tie-break.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ORDERS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "orders", "alias": "o", "fields": {"ID": {"table": "o", "column": "id", "type": "NUM"}, "CUSTOMER_ID": {"table": "o", "column": "customer_id", "type": "NUM"}, "AMOUNT": {"table": "o", "column": "amount", "type": "NUM"}, "NAME": {"table": "o", "column": "name", "type": "TEXT"}}},
 "CUSTOMERS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "customers", "alias": "c", "fields": {"ID": {"table": "c", "column": "id", "type": "NUM"}, "CNAME": {"table": "c", "column": "cname", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
ORDERS .> SORT_BY(_["amount"]) .> MAP(RECORD("name", _["name"], "amount", _["amount"])) .> SORT_BY(_["name"])
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:92
===

### name: review.order.link-over-sorted-rows-is-refused
--- note
orderDropped: a join returns its rows in no order, and SEL's are the left list's. Refused at
the LINK; Joining an unLIMITed ORDER BY derived table would lose the order.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ORDERS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "orders", "alias": "o", "fields": {"ID": {"table": "o", "column": "id", "type": "NUM"}, "CUSTOMER_ID": {"table": "o", "column": "customer_id", "type": "NUM"}, "AMOUNT": {"table": "o", "column": "amount", "type": "NUM"}, "NAME": {"table": "o", "column": "name", "type": "TEXT"}}},
 "CUSTOMERS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "customers", "alias": "c", "fields": {"ID": {"table": "c", "column": "id", "type": "NUM"}, "CNAME": {"table": "c", "column": "cname", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
ORDERS .> SORT_BY(_["amount"]) .> LINK(CUSTOMERS, _1["customer_id"] == _2["id"]) .> MAP(RECORD("a", _["amount"]))
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:35
===

### name: plan.hybrid.link-over-sorted-rows-joins-in-memory
--- note
orderDropped, planner side: the sorted rows come from SQL and the LINK runs in memory, not
a pure_sql join over a derived table that dropped its ORDER BY.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ORDERS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "orders", "alias": "o", "fields": {"ID": {"table": "o", "column": "id", "type": "NUM"}, "CUSTOMER_ID": {"table": "o", "column": "customer_id", "type": "NUM"}, "AMOUNT": {"table": "o", "column": "amount", "type": "NUM"}, "NAME": {"table": "o", "column": "name", "type": "TEXT"}}},
 "CUSTOMERS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "customers", "alias": "c", "fields": {"ID": {"table": "c", "column": "id", "type": "NUM"}, "CNAME": {"table": "c", "column": "cname", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- source
ORDERS .> SORT_BY(_["amount"]) .> LINK(CUSTOMERS, _1["customer_id"] == _2["id"]) .> MAP(RECORD("a", _["amount"]))
--- plan
hybrid
--- tables
orders
--- expect
SELECT `o`.* FROM `orders` `o` ORDER BY `o`.`amount` ASC
===

### name: plan.pure-memory.self-join-is-not-split
--- note
PHP-C9 / GO-C22: a continuation that starts at a LINK is fed under the source variable's own
name, so a LINK that reads that name again (a self-join) would find the truncated rows where
run() finds the whole relation. The split is not made.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ORDERS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "orders", "alias": "o", "fields": {"ID": {"table": "o", "column": "id", "type": "NUM"}, "CUSTOMER_ID": {"table": "o", "column": "customer_id", "type": "NUM"}, "AMOUNT": {"table": "o", "column": "amount", "type": "NUM"}, "NAME": {"table": "o", "column": "name", "type": "TEXT"}}},
 "CUSTOMERS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "customers", "alias": "c", "fields": {"ID": {"table": "c", "column": "id", "type": "NUM"}, "CNAME": {"table": "c", "column": "cname", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- source
ORDERS .> TAKE(4) .> LINK(ORDERS, _1["customer_id"] == _2["id"])
--- plan
pure_memory
--- tables
orders
===

### name: bind.value.null-element-is-refused
--- note
JS-C54b: a NULL element of a value binding has no SQL literal; it is a binding problem and a
refusal at the read. Rendering it as the empty string '' would be a wrong value.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"V1": {"kind": "value", "value": {"1": "a", "2": null}}, "XT": {"kind": "column", "column": "xt", "type": "TEXT"}}
--- source
ANY(V1, _ == XT)
--- error
E_SQL_BINDING 1:5
===

### name: register.dialect.backslash-escape-must-double-the-backslash
--- note
sql/MAP.md §3.1 (checkTextPairing): a textEscape whose values use a backslash escape must map
the backslash to itself doubled, or a value ending in a backslash un-escapes the doubled quote
on a backslash-reading server.
--- dialect
my-nl
--- register
[{"dialect": "my-nl", "extends": "mariadb", "version": "10.5", "lexical": {"textEscape": {"'": "''", "\n": "\\n"}}}]
--- source
"a"
--- throws
LogicException
===

### name: register.dialect.quote-escape-is-doubling-or-backslash
--- note
sql/MAP.md §3.1 (checkTextPairing): the quote is escaped by doubling it or with a backslash,
nothing else.
--- dialect
ansi-x
--- register
[{"dialect": "ansi-x", "extends": "ansi", "version": "2016", "lexical": {"textEscape": {"'": "x'", "x": "xx"}}}]
--- source
"a"
--- throws
LogicException
===

### name: bind.type.statement-is-not-declarable
--- note
DECLARABLE: LIST and STATEMENT are kinds of fragment a translation produces, not of a column.
A binding declared as one would read the column as UNKNOWN.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"XS": {"kind": "column", "column": "xs", "type": "STATEMENT"}}
--- source
XS > 1
--- error
E_SQL_BINDING
===

### name: norm.size.definition-past-the-budget-is-refused-at-the-assignment
--- note
expandedSize: a definition whose expanded tree passes the node budget is refused at that
assignment (docs/internals/sql-translation.md §7.4). The code is pinned and the position is not: sql/errors.md gives E_SQL_SIZE no position, and the hosts blame different nodes for E_SQL_DEPTH.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"XN": {"kind": "column", "column": "xn", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
X0 = XN; X1 = X0 + X0; X2 = X1 + X1; X3 = X2 + X2; X4 = X3 + X3; X5 = X4 + X4; X6 = X5 + X5; X7 = X6 + X6; X8 = X7 + X7; X9 = X8 + X8; X10 = X9 + X9; X11 = X10 + X10; X12 = X11 + X11; X13 = X12 + X12; X14 = X13 + X13; X15 = X14 + X14; X16 = X15 + X15; X17 = X16 + X16; X18 = X17 + X17; X19 = X18 + X18; X20 = X19 + X19; X21 = X20 + X20; X22 = X21 + X21; X23 = X22 + X22; X24 = X23 + X23; X24 > 0
--- error
E_SQL_SIZE
===

### name: norm.depth.definition-past-four-times-the-depth-is-refused-at-the-assignment
--- note
expandedSize: a definition taller than four times the evaluator's depth is refused (E_SQL_DEPTH). The code
is pinned and the position is not: the hosts blame different nodes of the chain (sql/errors.md
gives the code no position of its own).
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"XN": {"kind": "column", "column": "xn", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
X0 = XN; X1 = X0 + 1; X2 = X1 + 1; X3 = X2 + 1; X4 = X3 + 1; X5 = X4 + 1; X6 = X5 + 1; X7 = X6 + 1; X8 = X7 + 1; X9 = X8 + 1; X10 = X9 + 1; X11 = X10 + 1; X12 = X11 + 1; X13 = X12 + 1; X14 = X13 + 1; X15 = X14 + 1; X16 = X15 + 1; X17 = X16 + 1; X18 = X17 + 1; X19 = X18 + 1; X20 = X19 + 1; X21 = X20 + 1; X22 = X21 + 1; X23 = X22 + 1; X24 = X23 + 1; X25 = X24 + 1; X26 = X25 + 1; X27 = X26 + 1; X28 = X27 + 1; X29 = X28 + 1; X30 = X29 + 1; X31 = X30 + 1; X32 = X31 + 1; X33 = X32 + 1; X34 = X33 + 1; X35 = X34 + 1; X36 = X35 + 1; X37 = X36 + 1; X38 = X37 + 1; X39 = X38 + 1; X40 = X39 + 1; X41 = X40 + 1; X42 = X41 + 1; X43 = X42 + 1; X44 = X43 + 1; X45 = X44 + 1; X46 = X45 + 1; X47 = X46 + 1; X48 = X47 + 1; X49 = X48 + 1; X50 = X49 + 1; X51 = X50 + 1; X52 = X51 + 1; X53 = X52 + 1; X54 = X53 + 1; X55 = X54 + 1; X56 = X55 + 1; X57 = X56 + 1; X58 = X57 + 1; X59 = X58 + 1; X60 = X59 + 1; X61 = X60 + 1; X62 = X61 + 1; X63 = X62 + 1; X64 = X63 + 1; X65 = X64 + 1; X66 = X65 + 1; X67 = X66 + 1; X68 = X67 + 1; X69 = X68 + 1; X70 = X69 + 1; X71 = X70 + 1; X72 = X71 + 1; X73 = X72 + 1; X74 = X73 + 1; X75 = X74 + 1; X76 = X75 + 1; X77 = X76 + 1; X78 = X77 + 1; X79 = X78 + 1; X80 = X79 + 1; X81 = X80 + 1; X82 = X81 + 1; X83 = X82 + 1; X84 = X83 + 1; X85 = X84 + 1; X86 = X85 + 1; X87 = X86 + 1; X88 = X87 + 1; X89 = X88 + 1; X90 = X89 + 1; X91 = X90 + 1; X92 = X91 + 1; X93 = X92 + 1; X94 = X93 + 1; X95 = X94 + 1; X96 = X95 + 1; X97 = X96 + 1; X98 = X97 + 1; X99 = X98 + 1; X100 = X99 + 1; X101 = X100 + 1; X102 = X101 + 1; X103 = X102 + 1; X104 = X103 + 1; X105 = X104 + 1; X106 = X105 + 1; X107 = X106 + 1; X108 = X107 + 1; X109 = X108 + 1; X110 = X109 + 1; X111 = X110 + 1; X112 = X111 + 1; X113 = X112 + 1; X114 = X113 + 1; X115 = X114 + 1; X116 = X115 + 1; X117 = X116 + 1; X118 = X117 + 1; X119 = X118 + 1; X120 = X119 + 1; X121 = X120 + 1; X122 = X121 + 1; X123 = X122 + 1; X124 = X123 + 1; X125 = X124 + 1; X126 = X125 + 1; X127 = X126 + 1; X128 = X127 + 1; X129 = X128 + 1; X130 = X129 + 1;